course: dictionary
lesson: 865
title: Bike: a thing, or a thing you do
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one job. Bike can be a thing you can count, a bicycle with two wheels that you ride by pushing the pedals. It can also mean a motorbike. Bike can even be an action: to bike is to ride a bicycle. The context shows which job the word is doing.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat in the pads and rim, which is why they are hot after a long ride downhill.» Here bike is a thing, because it has brakes, pads and a rim. Ask: could I put a bicycle in this spot? If yes, bike is the thing.
explain: Now look for action words. If someone says «I will bike to school», the word bike is doing something, so it means to ride a bicycle. Its forms change like a verb: bikes, biked, biking. Check the verb form in the sentence to see when it happened.
explain: Safety words often come with bike. A bike helmet protects your head. A bike lane is a strip of road for riders. A bike path is a route away from cars. When you see bike in front of another word, the word after it names the thing it belongs to.
fact: Bike can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: A bike is a bicycle, a thing with two wheels that you ride by pushing pedals.
fact: A bike can also mean a motorbike, which has an engine.
fact: To bike means to ride a bicycle: «I bike to school» means «I ride my bicycle to school».
fact: Verb forms: bike, bikes, biked, biking. Words like «bike helmet», «bike lane» and «bike path» are useful phrases.
exercise: «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat in the pads and rim, which is why they are hot after a long ride downhill.» What is a bike in this sentence? | To ride a bicycle | A bike lane | A kind of puzzle | *A bicycle, a thing with two wheels
exercise: Mia says, «I will bike to school tomorrow.» What does bike mean here? | *To ride a bicycle | A strip of road for cyclists | To check the lights on a car | To buy a new helmet
exercise: «Take off scarves, bike helmets and anything with cords before playing on a climbing frame, because they can catch and strangle a child.» What are bike helmets? | Things that go on the pedals | Things you climb on | Things with cords that tie up | *Things you wear on your head to keep it safe
test: «A seat belt's lap part goes low across the hips, but a bike helmet sits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled.» Where should a bike helmet sit? | Under the chin, with no strap | Low across the hips | *Snug and level, just above the eyebrows | Around the neck, loose at the back
test: Yesterday Sam ___ to the park. Which word fits? | bike | bikes | biking | *biked
exam: In «these puzzles make you a chemistry detective, reading clues on a bike, a spoon, a candle or a kettle», what is a bike? | A ride with speed and time | A kind of chemistry puzzle | To ride a bicycle | *A thing with wheels, a bicycle
